                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5d6a8e16-f9cb-36d1-b0a3-06a613872c7e",
                        "entry_id": "89a7f0b7-333c-3dfb-b641-d738b527132d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "физ. явления, связанные с действием электрического тока; гальванические явления"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6b2099d-a848-4387-8d57-cc4e72955fd7",
                                "sense_id": "5d6a8e16-f9cb-36d1-b0a3-06a613872c7e",
                                "text": "Это какой-то труп из клиники, поднятый на ноги гальванизмом: даже и языком шевелит и как будто говорит что-то."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe7a3aea-0f91-3244-b1fd-f3439284181f",
                        "entry_id": "89a7f0b7-333c-3dfb-b641-d738b527132d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "раздел научной дисциплины об электричестве"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "390708f3-16f2-41c0-a133-4a4383c8a3ac",
                                "sense_id": "fe7a3aea-0f91-3244-b1fd-f3439284181f",
                                "text": "Явление, открытое Гальвани, было правильно объяснено Вольтом. Объяснение Гальвани было неверно, но «гальванизм» с неисчислимыми последствиями до учения об электричестве, открыт им…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc9471fc-945a-4516-872e-6ce9e26f5a4b",
                        "source_entry_id": "89a7f0b7-333c-3dfb-b641-d738b527132d",
                        "target_lang_word": "galvanism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "galvanism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2494463d-302a-3338-9320-be508c1f0557",
                                        "entry_id": "01de1733-9d94-3c60-9853-7e2ddbbe83bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The chemical generation of electricity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d44a507c-ae1f-3201-bd07-b7c9e91552e4",
                                        "entry_id": "01de1733-9d94-3c60-9853-7e2ddbbe83bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The (therapeutic) use of electricity directly applied to the body."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83bbf077-9f5b-4d5c-873a-7270e9db59e4",
                                                "sense_id": "d44a507c-ae1f-3201-bd07-b7c9e91552e4",
                                                "text": "Perhaps a corpse would be re-animated; galvanism had given token of such things: perhaps the component parts of a creature might be manufactured, brought together, and endued with vital warmth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab7f7192-f2c9-4a7e-97ee-9939e7eda9be",
                                                "sense_id": "d44a507c-ae1f-3201-bd07-b7c9e91552e4",
                                                "text": "The sudden application of galvanism to bands of savages may fairly rank as a new sensation, and they, thinking the wire held this strange and mysterious power, wisely left it alone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddd9eb36-3f05-487b-bb5b-feeb82c56893",
                                                "sense_id": "d44a507c-ae1f-3201-bd07-b7c9e91552e4",
                                                "text": "Erb and Remak in Germany, Beard and Rockwell and Althans in America, have used it with advantage, in the forms of galvanisms and faradisms, in the treatment of joint troubles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1c5e7226-7ad6-4000-b8a2-d9910027d66f",
                        "source_entry_id": "89a7f0b7-333c-3dfb-b641-d738b527132d",
